v31det: v30 + machine-independent time governance. The anneal core runs a FIXED iteration budget (hcFrac and all schedules iteration-based; wall clock demoted to a safety cap), then extends in fixed-size chunks while wall remains -- chunk count is the only machine-dependent quantity and best-so-far is monotone in it. Server results become locally replayable (enumerate chunk counts). Motive: same-seed local runs are byte-reproducible across our homogeneous nodes, but the server's different pacing produced 87,140 on P3 that no local run can replay -- a design flaw, not luck (flaw inventory in PIPELINE.md).
